abstract: >-
  This eight-module Lean 4.35.0 library formalizes the proper-divisor moment
  a(n) = sum over proper divisors d of d * tau(d) (OEIS A245211). Basic,
  Dominance, Families, Parity, OmegaFour, OmegaFive, OmegaSix, and TableCerts
  use no external Lean packages. The only positive fixed point with Omega(n) <=
  6 is 21, where Omega counts prime factors with multiplicity. OmegaFive
  excludes squarefree five-prime products by Cunningham forced closure. OmegaSix
  excludes all 11 exponent partitions of 6. Any other fixed point must be
  coprime to 6 and have Omega(n) >= 7. Lean also certifies the first 66 values,
  the minima 72 and 144 of A245213 and A245214, a(725) = 724, and uniqueness
  through 150. An independent Python sieve finds only 21 through 1,000,000. Its
  forced-closure search rejects all 14 candidate least primes for five distinct
  factors and all 30 for six.
